\": \"ASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase - The European Hematology Association (EHA)ASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4381, \"end\": 4440, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 59}, {\"start\": 4621, \"end\": 6162, \"excerpt_start\": 60, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n3 min read · July 23, 2026\\nJuly 23, 2026\\nShare\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nThe ASCERTAIN project is entering its final phase, with the final conference taking place on October 21, 2026 in Brussels.\\nASCERTAIN – Affordability and Sustainability improvements through new pricing, Cost- Effectiveness and ReimbursemenT models to Appraise INnovative health technologies – is an EU funded project focused on improving the affordability and accessibility of innovative health technologies by developing a policy support tool. EHA is a consortium partner in the project, which aligns with our advocacy priority to promote affordable and equitable access to innovative therapies in hematology.\\nAccessibility and pricing of new health technologies in hematology\\nHigh prices of new health technologies impede access to treatments for many patients with blood disorders. Health systems face the challenge of facilitating patient access to new health technologies while ensuring the system’s financial sustainability and providing incentives for innovation. Together with Myeloma Patients Europe and patient organizations for PNH and Sickle Cell Disease, EHA is representing the hematology field in the development of the ASCERTAIN project.\\nThe ASCERTAIN policy support tool\\nThe ASCERTAIN policy support tool aims to contribute to better anticipating and calculating pricing, health technology assessment (HTA), and reimbursement conditions for inno